{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses charged.</b> By the command of HaShem." "<b>And the elders of Israel.</b> He said thus to lighten [the burden], and likewise there are many, and I have already mentioned them." "<b>Observe all the commandment.</b> And what is it? — \"and you shall set up for yourself great stones,\" to contain the Torah. And the Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said that the number of commandments was written upon them, like those written in Halakhot Gedolot in the manner of warnings. And he spoke well."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {2 "גדולו' is an abbreviation for גדולות; resolved as 'great' modifying 'stones.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:58.761401550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}